WEBVTT

00:04.504 --> 00:05.922
<i>It all began</i>

00:06.965 --> 00:09.217
<i>with the Luminescent Baby that was born</i>

00:09.801 --> 00:11.469
<i>in Qing Qing City, China.</i>

00:12.220 --> 00:14.889
<i>Starting with this baby's birth,</i>

00:14.973 --> 00:18.560
<i>many began to manifest unique abilities</i>
<i>that were later named "Quirks".</i>

00:19.060 --> 00:22.272
<i>People born with special abilities</i>
<i>increased day by day.</i>

00:22.355 --> 00:23.690
<i>Currently,</i>

00:23.773 --> 00:26.151
<i>it has created a superhuman society</i>
<i>where approximately</i>

00:26.234 --> 00:29.070
<i>80% of the world's population</i>
<i>possesses some form of a Quirk.</i>

00:30.196 --> 00:33.366
<i>The profession that was born</i>
<i>in such a world filled with chaos</i>

00:33.450 --> 00:34.868
<i>was the job of a Hero.</i>

00:36.619 --> 00:39.581
<i>Under government sanction, Heroes utilize</i>

00:39.664 --> 00:42.667
<i>their effective Quirks to serve society.</i>

00:42.751 --> 00:44.377
<i>They are the chosen ones.</i>

00:46.504 --> 00:48.131
<i>But at this point in time,</i>

00:48.214 --> 00:50.341
<i>there are Heroes who are not like that.</i>

00:51.092 --> 00:52.594
<i>They are not chosen,</i>

00:52.677 --> 00:56.014
<i>and volunteer to operate independently.</i>
<i>They are Illegal Heroes.</i>

00:57.098 --> 00:59.225
<i>What is their meaning of "Justice"?</i>

01:01.895 --> 01:03.438
<i>Can they even</i>

01:03.521 --> 01:06.107
<i>be called Heroes to begin with?</i>

01:09.069 --> 01:09.903
<i>This</i>

01:10.528 --> 01:14.449
<i>is what happened before Izuku Midoriya</i>
<i>entered U.A. High School.</i>

01:14.532 --> 01:17.118
<i>It's a story about Vigilantes who strived</i>

01:17.202 --> 01:19.245
<i>to become real Heroes.</i>

02:52.088 --> 02:53.798
VIGILANTE
A CRIME PREVENTION ORGANIZATION

02:53.882 --> 02:55.758
THAT OPERATES OUTSIDE OF LEGAL PROCEDURES
A VIGILANTE GROUP

02:55.842 --> 02:57.594
ALSO REFERS TO MEMBERS OF VIGILANTE GROUPS
WHO ENCOURAGE VIGILANTISM

03:05.852 --> 03:07.145
He's going crazy.

03:07.228 --> 03:08.646
Run!

03:08.730 --> 03:10.106
Food, food.

03:13.359 --> 03:14.944
My teeth are my life.

03:16.696 --> 03:17.780
My motorcycle!

03:17.864 --> 03:20.074
-Oh no!
-It's all right now.

03:22.535 --> 03:23.494
Why?

03:24.412 --> 03:26.164
Because I am here!

03:28.207 --> 03:32.337
Take this, Villain! Detroit Smash!

03:35.173 --> 03:36.216
Wow! All Might!

03:36.299 --> 03:37.634
It only took one hit!

03:37.717 --> 03:39.636
He's the number one Hero after all.

03:44.098 --> 03:45.725
Is everyone all right?

03:46.559 --> 03:48.019
I hope no one is hurt.

03:50.813 --> 03:53.858
The same can't be said for you.
Later, take care.

03:59.864 --> 04:04.452
All Might. It's so amazing
to see him in person!

04:06.663 --> 04:07.956
Oh crap!

04:08.039 --> 04:09.749
I'll be late to university!

04:16.839 --> 04:18.132
I'm sorry!

04:19.509 --> 04:21.886
What are you going to do about this, huh?

04:23.096 --> 04:25.890
I just bought this. Apologize.

04:28.518 --> 04:29.394
Grovel.

04:31.062 --> 04:32.689
I'm very sorry!

04:34.148 --> 04:35.400
He really groveled!

04:35.483 --> 04:37.151
Do you have no pride?

04:37.735 --> 04:38.569
Weakling.

04:44.867 --> 04:46.077
You little…

04:48.329 --> 04:51.249
-How dare you!
-You bastard!

04:54.294 --> 04:55.545
Stop right there!

04:55.628 --> 04:57.338
<i>Koichi Haimawari.</i>

04:57.422 --> 05:00.258
<i>A normal university student</i>
<i>who's always working his part-time job.</i>

05:00.341 --> 05:02.302
<i>His Quirk is Slide and Glide.</i>

05:02.385 --> 05:04.470
<i>He can travel by sliding.</i>

05:04.554 --> 05:05.388
QUIRK
SLIDE AND GLIDE

05:05.471 --> 05:06.472
<i>To activate his Quirk,</i>

05:06.556 --> 05:09.183
<i>he needs to touch a surface</i>
<i>in at least three places.</i>

05:09.767 --> 05:10.977
<i>But as for his speed,</i>

05:11.936 --> 05:14.105
<i>it's about as fast as a bicycle.</i>

05:14.647 --> 05:16.065
Oh, a transportation type of Quirk.

05:16.149 --> 05:17.734
That's pretty useful.

05:17.817 --> 05:19.902
But it's not that fast.

05:19.986 --> 05:22.488
It's a little creepy.
Almost like a cockroach.

05:22.572 --> 05:24.032
<i>Leave me alone!</i>

05:31.247 --> 05:34.042
<i>With a pop heart</i>

05:34.667 --> 05:37.336
<i>And a pop beat</i>

05:37.420 --> 05:40.548
<i>Sending my love to you</i>

05:40.631 --> 05:43.426
<i>Pop with Hip the Hop</i>

05:43.509 --> 05:48.306
Thanks for coming, everyone!

05:49.223 --> 05:51.267
<i>That smile</i>

05:51.350 --> 05:53.728
<i>You showed me that day</i>

05:53.811 --> 05:56.147
<i>I've been wanting to see it again</i>

05:56.230 --> 06:00.359
<i>I've been searching for it</i>

06:01.319 --> 06:04.197
<i>I'm always thinking of you</i>

06:04.280 --> 06:06.699
<i>Using my voice as a guide</i>

06:07.325 --> 06:09.869
<i>For you to find me</i>

06:09.952 --> 06:13.623
<i>For you to hold me tight</i>

06:14.749 --> 06:18.377
<i>Shine</i>

06:18.461 --> 06:21.672
<i>Sparkle</i>

06:21.756 --> 06:24.842
<i>P-O-P S-T-E-P</i>

06:24.926 --> 06:28.971
<i>Let it reach you, and shine</i>

06:30.098 --> 06:32.975
<i>Sparkle</i>

06:34.060 --> 06:36.687
This is Pop Step's guerilla gig, huh?

06:37.271 --> 06:39.774
I hope she doesn't get caught
by the police.

06:39.857 --> 06:43.736
<i>Her songs aren't that memorable,</i>
<i>and her flashy make-up is hiding her face.</i>

06:44.445 --> 06:47.990
<i>But at that moment,</i>
<i>she was shining so brightly</i>

06:48.699 --> 06:50.284
<i>because she was leaping across the sky.</i>

06:50.827 --> 06:53.746
Must be nice to have a leaping Quirk.

06:55.039 --> 06:57.333
Oh crap! I have to go to work!

07:10.680 --> 07:13.975
<i>Humans have longing for things</i>
<i>that are high above reach.</i>

07:15.268 --> 07:16.561
<i>But anything below their eye level</i>

07:17.145 --> 07:19.772
<i>tends to literally be looked down upon.</i>

07:27.530 --> 07:28.948
<i>Life</i>

07:29.991 --> 07:31.451
<i>is so unfair.</i>

07:32.493 --> 07:35.371
I'll be docking your pay
for the amount of time you were late.

07:35.455 --> 07:36.622
Okay.

07:36.706 --> 07:38.791
<i>In the end, I was late.</i>

07:40.084 --> 07:41.627
-Welcome.
-Damn it.

07:41.711 --> 07:43.796
The next time I see him…

07:44.964 --> 07:46.966
It's the cockroach.

07:49.969 --> 07:50.803
CLINK

07:51.471 --> 07:55.641
My Quirk is called Spike.
Getting stabbed by this will hurt.

07:56.642 --> 07:58.102
Are you scared?

08:00.480 --> 08:01.481
Take this.

08:02.231 --> 08:03.649
Loser.

08:11.949 --> 08:12.783
Damn it.

08:13.659 --> 08:15.203
What was up with those guys?

08:15.286 --> 08:17.246
Why aren't the police arresting them?

08:17.330 --> 08:20.082
It's making me so mad. How irritating.

08:21.209 --> 08:22.460
<i>I've decided.</i>

08:24.003 --> 08:26.255
<i>I'm going to do that tonight.</i>

08:27.131 --> 08:29.967
<i>I'll change into my special costume,</i>

08:30.051 --> 08:32.428
<i>use my Quirk to the fullest,</i>

08:34.222 --> 08:35.848
<i>and feel refreshed!</i>

08:35.932 --> 08:37.892
<i>Forget the law.</i>

08:37.975 --> 08:40.269
<i>I'm going to randomly choose my target!</i>

08:40.353 --> 08:42.104
<i>Oh, I found my target.</i>

08:44.190 --> 08:45.274
You dropped this.

08:46.526 --> 08:48.819
The bus stop for the sleeper bus
is that way.

08:49.779 --> 08:52.365
The last train leaves in ten minutes.

08:59.539 --> 09:01.791
Nice Guy is working hard again.

09:01.874 --> 09:04.377
Wow, Nice is so nice.

09:04.460 --> 09:06.879
Thanks, Nice Guy.

09:06.963 --> 09:07.922
Good job, Nice Guy.

09:09.507 --> 09:11.759
Please take out our trash
while you're at it.

09:13.928 --> 09:16.806
Doing good deeds feels amazing!

09:17.932 --> 09:21.060
I'm so tired and thirsty.

09:21.143 --> 09:22.770
Here you go.

09:22.853 --> 09:24.397
Thanks.

09:25.565 --> 09:27.149
Wait, who are you?

09:27.233 --> 09:29.944
Pop Step? Why are you here?

09:30.611 --> 09:34.198
You're the one who's going around town
picking up trash, right?

09:34.282 --> 09:36.409
Your name is…

09:36.492 --> 09:38.786
-Cockroach Guy.
-It's Nice Guy.

09:39.787 --> 09:40.663
That lame hoodie

09:41.330 --> 09:43.749
-is to cosplay as All Might, right?
-Yeah.

09:44.709 --> 09:48.629
I'm striving to imitate him
by being useful to society.

09:49.255 --> 09:51.340
Plus, this isn't lame. It's cool.

09:53.175 --> 09:56.512
I see. You're the type that knows
your place in life, huh?

09:56.596 --> 09:58.222
Yes, yes, call it what you like.

09:58.306 --> 10:00.433
-But that's important too.
-Know-Your-Place Guy.

10:00.516 --> 10:01.767
It's Nice Guy!

10:03.227 --> 10:05.313
Don't get too carried away with your

10:05.396 --> 10:07.773
make-believe idol act,
or you'll get caught by the police.

10:07.857 --> 10:09.233
Oh, and thanks for the juice.

10:09.317 --> 10:10.610
Hey!

10:10.693 --> 10:14.155
I'm not a make-believe idol.
I'm the real deal!

10:16.490 --> 10:17.867
What the hell was that for?

10:18.868 --> 10:22.413
What's with this girl? She's wearing
a revealing outfit under her coat.

10:23.247 --> 10:25.875
-She's a pervert.
-I know her.

10:25.958 --> 10:29.211
She's the pathetic girl known online
as the ass-baring high schooler.

10:29.295 --> 10:32.131
Is this face paint supposed
to make you look like a hero?

10:32.214 --> 10:33.424
Aren't you a villain?

10:34.008 --> 10:36.636
Stop it. I don't reveal my real face
to the public!

10:36.719 --> 10:39.764
Then let's take a picture of her real face
and post it online.

10:40.765 --> 10:42.683
-Wow, you're mean.
-Hey.

10:42.767 --> 10:44.352
Stop it, you guys.

10:45.478 --> 10:47.855
What? This is none of your business.

10:47.938 --> 10:49.982
Get lost, Lame Hoodie.

10:50.066 --> 10:51.692
Uh… Well…

10:52.193 --> 10:53.361
It's not lame.

10:53.444 --> 10:54.862
What?

10:55.905 --> 10:58.115
You're right, this is none of my business.

10:58.658 --> 11:00.076
Sorry.

11:00.159 --> 11:01.744
Stop it!

11:04.497 --> 11:06.832
I'm not Lame Hoodie.

11:06.916 --> 11:08.459
I'm not Know-Your-Place Guy either.

11:08.542 --> 11:12.213
I'm someone who won't abandon
those in need of help.

11:12.296 --> 11:13.756
I'm Nice Guy!

11:14.799 --> 11:16.384
<i>Although I'm not a good fighter.</i>

11:16.967 --> 11:18.677
What did you say?

11:18.761 --> 11:20.346
<i>Time for a surprise attack.</i>

11:22.264 --> 11:25.101
What the hell are you doing?

11:28.938 --> 11:31.482
Hey, I've actually seen you before.

11:32.316 --> 11:34.944
Why are you meddling in our business?

11:35.694 --> 11:38.531
A cockroach trying to play a hero, huh?

11:39.281 --> 11:42.284
-Ouch!
-All right, I've decided.

11:42.952 --> 11:44.703
You'll get more than a beating.

11:44.787 --> 11:48.457
I'll destroy you along
with that convenience store!

11:50.251 --> 11:51.669
While we're at it,

11:51.752 --> 11:54.797
we'll strip this pervert naked too.

11:57.216 --> 11:59.844
Why? Why would you do something like that?

11:59.927 --> 12:03.931
Because you got me angry as hell,
that's why!

12:04.807 --> 12:08.102
Stop it! I'll call the police!

12:08.185 --> 12:10.688
Wouldn't it be better
to call in the Heroes instead?

12:10.771 --> 12:13.858
Say, "Help me, All Might!"

12:13.941 --> 12:15.443
Come on, say it.

12:17.653 --> 12:19.905
<i>All Might is busy.</i>

12:20.990 --> 12:22.199
Cat got your tongue?

12:25.536 --> 12:29.290
<i>No matter how much we need help right now,</i>

12:32.251 --> 12:33.794
<i>he wouldn't come flying…</i>

12:35.629 --> 12:38.757
-What?
-A human came crashing down!

12:41.927 --> 12:46.307
Were you guys talking about All Might?

12:46.390 --> 12:47.892
He won't be coming here.

12:49.894 --> 12:50.728
But…

12:52.521 --> 12:54.231
I'm here!

12:57.026 --> 13:00.696
That was a bit of a clumsy landing,
but no worries.

13:00.779 --> 13:04.492
When in rush, a garbage dump
serves as a great cushion.

13:05.117 --> 13:07.369
Also, by training your neck,

13:07.453 --> 13:11.457
you can reduce the risk
of cervical spine injury and concussion.

13:12.082 --> 13:13.876
What's up with you,

13:14.376 --> 13:15.377
old man--?

13:21.800 --> 13:24.428
-Who the hell are you?
-What are you doing all of a sudden?

13:25.054 --> 13:27.556
"Who are you?"
and "What are you planning to do?".

13:28.057 --> 13:30.267
I'll answer those questions for you.

13:32.061 --> 13:35.981
My name is Knuckleduster.

13:36.607 --> 13:40.194
I'm a cleaner who specializes
in getting rid of scums like you guys.

13:41.820 --> 13:45.074
I'm going to kill you--

13:48.786 --> 13:51.288
No discoloration.

13:51.872 --> 13:54.667
This isn't the one. Next.

14:03.551 --> 14:05.844
He's not the one either.

14:06.512 --> 14:07.972
Hey, kid!

14:09.056 --> 14:11.642
I have nothing to do
with those guys at all.

14:11.725 --> 14:14.186
You're promising.

14:14.895 --> 14:17.648
I need an extra hand.
Help me with my work.

14:17.731 --> 14:19.775
I'll make you a Hero.

14:21.277 --> 14:25.489
I'm not interested in that.
I'll be going now.

14:27.408 --> 14:28.659
You're lying.

14:29.285 --> 14:32.913
You respect All Might,
and your hobby is to help people.

14:32.997 --> 14:36.625
But you're telling me that you're
not interested in becoming a Hero?

14:37.543 --> 14:38.878
Well… But…

14:38.961 --> 14:42.631
With my lame Quirk, I wouldn't qualify
to get a Pro Hero license.

14:44.216 --> 14:45.676
So what?

14:46.343 --> 14:47.678
Well…

14:47.761 --> 14:50.556
"Powerful Quirks" and "Pro Hero license".

14:50.639 --> 14:54.143
Those things have nothing to do
with true justice.

14:55.060 --> 14:57.229
When faced with something
that requires your attention,

14:57.313 --> 14:59.565
will you take action or not?

14:59.648 --> 15:03.652
That's the only thing that matters
to those with the soul of a Hero.

15:04.236 --> 15:07.615
<i>Basically, that means this old man</i>
<i>is unlicensed?</i>

15:10.993 --> 15:14.830
What a joke. Why are you babbling on
about justice, you old man!

15:14.914 --> 15:16.790
Stop that.

15:16.874 --> 15:20.127
I won't go easy on you
just because you're holding a hostage.

15:20.210 --> 15:22.421
She's not a hostage.

15:22.504 --> 15:26.008
I'm going to rip her face apart
with my Spike!

15:27.217 --> 15:28.218
Otherwise,

15:28.302 --> 15:31.138
I can't release this anger!

15:32.306 --> 15:35.100
<i>When faced with something</i>
<i>that requires your attention…</i>

15:35.184 --> 15:36.685
Stop it!

15:36.769 --> 15:39.188
<i>Will you take action or not?</i>

15:39.271 --> 15:41.899
<i>That's the only thing that matters</i>

15:41.982 --> 15:44.401
<i>to those with the soul of a Hero.</i>

15:52.910 --> 15:55.496
Good job, Kid!

16:10.719 --> 16:13.305
In the end, none of them
were who I was looking for.

16:13.389 --> 16:16.350
But let's check his ID just in case.

16:21.605 --> 16:22.481
Kid.

16:22.564 --> 16:26.360
I'll teach you everything about
the satisfying job of being a Hero.

16:27.444 --> 16:30.572
Punching evil people is exhilarating.

16:32.533 --> 16:35.828
I absolutely decline.

16:36.620 --> 16:38.789
<i>The thoughts going through my head</i>
<i>at that moment</i>

16:38.872 --> 16:41.417
<i>weren't "Thank you" or "You saved me",</i>

16:42.626 --> 16:44.545
<i>but it was, "Someone even crazier</i>

16:45.295 --> 16:46.380
<i>has appeared."</i>

16:47.339 --> 16:50.592
<i>And as for that crazy guy…</i>

16:51.218 --> 16:53.971
Koichi Haimawari, 19 years old.

16:54.054 --> 16:55.931
First year at Hitonami University.

16:56.015 --> 16:58.934
Hey! That's my student ID!
Why do you have my wallet?

16:59.518 --> 17:00.978
I'm going to call you Koichi.

17:01.061 --> 17:03.313
Or would you prefer Nice Guy?

17:03.814 --> 17:05.774
Stop looking through my things!

17:05.858 --> 17:07.776
Call me Master.

17:07.860 --> 17:10.487
Like I already said,
I won't be your apprentice.

17:10.571 --> 17:13.490
In fact, please leave my house.

17:14.616 --> 17:17.828
What? You only have barley tea
in your fridge?

17:18.829 --> 17:20.497
Oh, you have beer.

17:20.581 --> 17:22.499
That's for when the upperclassmen
come to visit.

17:22.583 --> 17:25.878
This is not allowed for a kid like you.
I'm confiscating it.

17:25.961 --> 17:28.297
<i>He's not listening to me at all!</i>

17:31.717 --> 17:34.094
Damn it, that bastard.

17:34.178 --> 17:38.849
I'm going to kill that cockroach dude
and that violent old man.

17:38.932 --> 17:42.061
No, we shouldn't get involved
with him anymore.

17:46.440 --> 17:48.275
Those are nasty injuries.

17:49.693 --> 17:51.070
Who the hell are you?

17:52.571 --> 17:56.784
I have great medicine to give you guys.

17:56.867 --> 18:01.747
I'm searching for a drug
that's been circulating in this city.

18:02.831 --> 18:04.666
What? A drug?

18:09.463 --> 18:11.131
It's new and dangerous.

18:12.299 --> 18:14.885
The drug is called Trigger.

18:15.677 --> 18:17.846
<i>It weakens the user's sense of reason,</i>

18:17.930 --> 18:20.015
<i>while boosting their Quirks.</i>

18:21.016 --> 18:24.353
<i>In other words, it's a drug</i>
<i>that turns civilians into Villains.</i>

18:32.277 --> 18:34.321
This is amazing!

18:35.322 --> 18:38.951
At this rate, this city will be filled
with off-the-cuff Villains.

18:39.660 --> 18:40.911
We can't let this be.

18:41.411 --> 18:45.624
But shouldn't we leave this up
to the Heroes and the police?

18:45.707 --> 18:46.875
I can't count on them.

18:47.793 --> 18:49.795
<i>These Villains created by Trigger</i>

18:49.878 --> 18:52.381
<i>appear in front of crowds out of nowhere.</i>

18:52.464 --> 18:56.802
<i>Both the police and Pro Heroes</i>
<i>will always be one step behind.</i>

18:57.511 --> 18:59.930
This is where we come in.

19:00.013 --> 19:02.224
Did you just say "we"?

19:02.307 --> 19:05.686
That's right. You and I
will stop suspicious individuals

19:05.769 --> 19:07.104
and check their tongues.

19:07.187 --> 19:08.230
Tongue?

19:08.313 --> 19:11.650
<i>Trigger users suffer a side-effect</i>
<i>that changes the color of their tongues.</i>

19:12.192 --> 19:13.986
<i>It turns black.</i>

19:15.487 --> 19:18.198
That's why you were checking
their tongues?

19:18.282 --> 19:19.658
That's right.

19:19.741 --> 19:22.411
We'll give an instant beating
to anyone with a black tongue,

19:22.494 --> 19:24.329
get the name of their dealer,

19:24.413 --> 19:26.582
and stop the drug circulation
right from the roots!

19:27.541 --> 19:29.418
You're going to beat them up
without warning?

19:29.501 --> 19:30.794
We have to take initiative!

19:31.545 --> 19:34.631
We have to settle this before junkies
shoot themselves up with Trigger!

19:34.715 --> 19:37.843
I feel like no one
will let us see their tongues.

19:37.926 --> 19:40.804
We'll beat up anyone suspicious
who refuses to comply with us!

19:42.723 --> 19:44.641
Your jokes are kind of intense…

19:44.725 --> 19:46.268
I wished it was a joke!

19:46.351 --> 19:49.438
But he wasn't joking at all!

19:51.231 --> 19:52.858
What's all the fuss?

19:53.358 --> 19:55.235
Pop Step!

19:55.819 --> 19:57.863
Well, the thing is…

20:00.490 --> 20:02.701
You're looking for junkies
and dealers, huh?

20:03.827 --> 20:05.287
Thanks for yesterday, by the way.

20:05.370 --> 20:09.374
But I haven't forgotten the fact
that you tried to abandon me, Old Man.

20:10.876 --> 20:12.628
Suit yourself.

20:13.128 --> 20:15.589
-Anyways, Nice Guy…
-Just call me Koichi.

20:16.340 --> 20:19.092
Is that your real name?
Okay, I'll call you Koichi.

20:19.176 --> 20:21.511
Why are you helping out this guy?

20:24.848 --> 20:26.892
What was that pause just now?

20:28.644 --> 20:32.356
Because he'll go around punching everyone
if I don't stop him.

20:32.439 --> 20:35.651
I'm only punching
the ones that look suspicious.

20:35.734 --> 20:37.527
Like those players out in the street.

20:37.611 --> 20:40.948
Are you serious? You're just winging it?

20:41.031 --> 20:43.492
You guys need to use your head.

20:44.243 --> 20:45.994
People most definitely

20:46.078 --> 20:48.622
take pictures of Villains
who appear in the city.

20:48.705 --> 20:50.624
Search "A never-before-seen Villain"

20:50.707 --> 20:54.711
or "Sudden Villain appearance"
and try to find out the location.

20:54.795 --> 20:56.838
You should start questioning people
after that.

20:56.922 --> 20:58.715
-You're so smart.
-Hey!

20:58.799 --> 20:59.925
You right there!

21:00.634 --> 21:01.843
Show me your tongue!

21:02.552 --> 21:04.263
Stop right there!

21:04.346 --> 21:07.266
He's obviously a normal office worker!

21:07.349 --> 21:08.225
Show me your tongue!

21:14.022 --> 21:15.232
So sorry.

21:16.066 --> 21:18.443
Are those figures for children?

21:18.527 --> 21:22.322
A grown adult is walking around
with dolls? How suspicious.

21:22.406 --> 21:24.908
There are so many people
with hobbies like that!

21:24.992 --> 21:28.745
My job is to sell toys.

21:28.829 --> 21:31.373
See? He's just an honest worker.

21:31.456 --> 21:33.083
I'll confirm that right now.

21:33.166 --> 21:35.294
First, I'll make sure
you don't give me trouble.

21:38.922 --> 21:41.800
Acts of violence in public.

21:42.301 --> 21:43.510
That's not very civil.

21:44.386 --> 21:48.265
Are you one of the Instant Villains
that are commonly seen these days?

21:48.974 --> 21:50.392
You're…

21:51.018 --> 21:54.187
Erasure Hero. Eraser Head.

23:26.780 --> 23:28.782
<i>Hello. I'm Koichi Haimawari.</i>

23:28.865 --> 23:31.076
<i>I'm unlicensed, but I started</i>
<i>carrying out Hero duties.</i>

23:31.785 --> 23:33.745
<i>My Hero name is The Crawler.</i>

23:33.829 --> 23:36.832
<i>I'm about to get involved</i>
<i>in a big incident.</i>

23:36.915 --> 23:38.834
<i>Next episode, "Takeoff".</i>

23:38.917 --> 23:40.460
<i>I want to leap across the sky too!</i>

23:40.544 --> 23:41.628
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita
